{"id": "002", "parent": "001", "decision": "adopt", "reasons": ["success is higher by +0.083 (interval -0.010 to +0.198): 3 tasks better, 1 worse, p = 0.004", "still below the bar: pass^k = 0.7188, needs >= 0.9"], "note": "Refund requests without an order number now use the existing model call to extract the product phrase the customer used. The harness applies its existing refund rules only if that phrase matches exactly one order on the identified account; otherwise it asks for the order number. This should fix the missing-order-number failures for eligible, already-refunded, late, and undelivered purchases. If a refund response is lost, the retry uses the existing receipt for that case rather than issuing another refund. I reviewed the changes against the reference code but did not run the workflow.\n", "files": [{"path": "support_steps.py", "added": 54, "removed": 11}, {"path": "workflow.yaml", "added": 8, "removed": 0}], "tree": "9fd55c78d0c4", "improver": {"note": "", "cost_usd": 0.14122, "seconds": 91.7421621249996, "model": "gpt-6.2-sol", "denied": [], "error": null}, "dev": {"success": 0.8125, "pass^k": 0.8125, "violations": 0, "cost_per_task": 0.0021143541666666667, "latency_p95": 2.82, "tokens_per_task": 877.21875, "success_ci": [0.6875, 0.9166666666666666], "k": 2, "failing": ["two-address-allowed-refund-refused", "two-address-and-language", "two-refund-allowed-address-refused", "two-refund-allowed-refund-refused", "two-refund-and-address", "two-refund-and-emails", "unusual-change-email", "unusual-refund-status", "unusual-where-is-order"]}, "val": {"success": 0.7395833333333334, "pass^k": 0.71875, "violations": 0, "cost_per_task": 0.0021476875, "latency_p95": 2.803, "tokens_per_task": 886.34375, "success_ci": [0.59375, 0.875], "k": 3, "failing": ["v-two-billing-and-marketing", "v-two-both-refused", "v-two-language-allowed-refund-refused", "v-two-refund-allowed-cancelled-refused", "v-two-refund-and-incomplete-address", "v-two-refund-and-sms", "v-unusual-a